  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this view",
      "items": [
        "Each row is an independent guarded transition, not a chronological sequence across rows. Repeated phase labels name the same underlying phase; aliases prevent unrelated rules from sharing ambiguous drawing corridors. The normal-procedure view supplies the connected happy path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading this view",
      "items": [
        "snake_case labels are real session.phase strings. Nodes in the 'conceptual step' legend group, or with tag 'conceptual'/'phase group', are not phase strings.",
        "Pilot calls move a phase only after telemetry confirms the claim (_at_hold, _at_crossing, _lined_up). Take-off, landing and vacating come from the mission track alone (airfield.py 44-50)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Rules",
      "items": [
        "Without a published pattern, downwind and base are refused and the pilot reports final directly from inbound (1845-1856).",
        "A runway change, or an altimeter change while in arrival_briefing, rebriefs the arrival. Any landing grant is freed and prefixed with 'go around' (1005-1017).",
        "Landing revocation (timeout, occupied runway, tower loss) and the pilot's go-around call both free the lane and run _reentry (1114-1116, 1858-1865). A go-around during an unconfirmed touchdown is refused while the track is on the ground (1862-1863)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Transition evidence (file lines)",
      "items": [
        "inbound \u2192 final: no pattern, or straight in (1855-1856)",
        "rebrief: rebrief (1005-1017)",
        "arrival_briefing \u2192 inbound_standby: 599-600, 1134-1137",
        "go around: revoked or pilot call (1114-1116, 1858-1865)",
        "touch-and-go: touch-and-go: lane freed (840-841, 901-904); landed airborne again 827-828",
        "re-entry outcomes: 926-938"
      ]
    }
  ]
